According to [RBI/DOR/2025-26/340], an NBFC requires prior written permission from the Reserve Bank for certain acquisitions of shareholding or control. Specifically, prior permission is required for: 
(1) any takeover or acquisition of control of the NBFC, which may or may not result in change of management [RBI/DOR/2025-26/340];
(2) any change in the shareholding of the NBFC, including progressive increases over time, which would result in acquisition/transfer of shareholding of 26 percent or more of the paid-up equity capital of the NBFC [RBI/DOR/2025-26/340];
(3) any change in the shareholding of an HFC accepting/holding public deposits, including progressive increases over time, which would result in acquisition/transfer of shareholding of 10 percent or more of the paid-up equity capital of the HFC by/to a foreign investor [RBI/DOR/2025-26/340];
(4) any change in the shareholding pattern/capital structure of a SPD, which requires prior approval of the Reserve Bank [RBI/DOR/2025-26/340].

